	(text "Power board of a cable-free key module (spec 2b), in the battery rail. Pack: 4, 5 or 6 AA, NiMH or alkaline, 4.0 to about 10 V, on J1.\nF1 1.5 A hold at 23 C, 1.08 A at 50 C (user, 2026-11-14; worst case 0.85 A: LEDs at the cap on a 4.0 V pack). Q1 blocks a reversed pack (gate to GND through 100 k; |VGS| = pack voltage, 12 V absolute maximum).\nD1 clamps its gate (10 V Zener, conducts only above a fresh alkaline pack); C20 damps the ringing when the pack is plugged in.\nSW1 is the on / off switch: it carries no load current (third contact unused). On: VSW = VPACK feeds the cut-off divider on the 3.3 V converter's enable and the pack divider.\nCut-off (review): R2 / 330 k on the precise enable (1.0 V rising, 0.9 V falling) = on at 1.0 V per cell, off at 0.9 V per cell. R2 = 1.65 M: 6 cells, as delivered.\n4 cells (numpad): bridge JP1, which puts 2.55 M in parallel (1.0 M). One board for every module (user). Off: VSW pulled to GND by the dividers, both converters in shutdown (the pod is dead, so EN_5V is low); 3 to 13 uA left (shutdown currents, 85 C worst case).\nU1 TPS629210: MODE/S-CONF 27.4 k = VSET mode, auto PFM/PWM with AEE, up to 2.5 MHz, output discharge on; FB/VSET open = 3.3 V; 2.2 uH, 22 uF; 4 uA quiescent.\nU2 TPS630701 (fixed 5.0 V): FB on VOUT, VSEL low, PS/SYNC high through 100 k = power save, 1.5 uH, 2 x 22 uF, VAUX 100 nF; a 10 uF 0603 at the VIN pins and one (C8) at the VOUT pins, as the datasheet. Enabled only by EN_5V from the pod\n(1 k in series, 100 k pull-down: off by default). U3 TPS2553 caps the LED rail: RILIM 49.9 k = 475-565 mA, constant current (not latching); FAULT is not wired; 100 nF at its IN pin.\nPack divider 2.2 M / 680 k: 10 V -> 2.36 V at the pod's ADC pin (100 nF there); the two dividers draw 2.5 + 3.6 uA at 7.2 V while the switch is on.\nLead J2 (JST GH, 1 A per contact, 1:1 to the pod): 1 +5V_LED, 2 GND, 3 EN_5V, 4 VBAT_SENSE, 5 GND, 6 +3V3.\nBoard: tools/pcb_pod.py, 48 x 22 mm in the rear leg of the battery rail (27 mm deep; user)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
